                            <comment id="16472104" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 11 May 2018 15:24:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I made changes for &lt;tt&gt;IgniteAtomicSequence&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;IgniteCountDownLatch&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;IgniteSemaphore&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;IgniteLock&lt;/tt&gt;. This data structures are vulnerable to a race condition. &lt;tt&gt;IgniteAtomicLong&lt;/tt&gt; was fixed before by ticket &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7845&quot; title=&quot;Data race on atomicLong close&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-7845&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-7845&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;IgniteSet&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;IgniteQueue&lt;/tt&gt; makes requests to distributed cache when we try to get these data structures, so it&apos;s not necessary to fix tests for these structures.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
